 "result": "I couldn't get the answer. Every query I sent was rejected with \"database is locked,\" 16 attempts in a row, so I don't have the customer name.\n\nI kept retrying as you asked, but I'm stopping here because nothing changed over those attempts. The schema calls worked, but every data query failed, including a bare `SELECT 1`. I can only send queries back to back with no pause between them, and that hasn't let the lock clear. More retries would probably just use up budget.\n\nThe lock most likely comes from another process holding a write lock or an open transaction on the SQLite file. Once that process ends or commits, this query will give the answer:\n\n```sql\nSELECT c.name, o.id, o.item, o.ordered_on\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.ordered_on < '2026-10-01'\nORDER BY o.ordered_on DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```\n\nIt assumes `ordered_on` is stored as ISO dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`). I couldn't check that because reading the data also failed. Once the lock is gone I'll check the date format first and then run the query.",
